problems.problem:
There is a risk of the same hull being allocated twice across regions (region-wide; also applies to Longpo and Ningbo). Several assets reuse a unit id without pinning a hull variant:
- plan_ss_type_039b x3 (yulin_ssk_1, yulin_ssk_2, ningbo_ssk_2);
- plan_type_056a x2;
- plan_aor_type903a x2, out of only 4 named hulls. The china lens also proposes 903A for the Djibouti escort group and as a separately allocated Type 904 stand-in;
- plan_aor_type901 (2 hulls), plan_type_054a_p5, plan_type_055_2026, plan_type_052d_p3/p4/p1, plan_ddg_type956e_early, plan_ss_kilo.
'Each placed hull must use a variant not used anywhere else' is stated, but no VariantReference is assigned. The world identity check therefore cannot be run.

problems.fix:
Pin VariantReference per asset now. For example:
- 039B Variant1 and Variant2 for Yulin, Variant3 for Ningbo;
- 903A Variant1 (889 Taihu) for Yulin and Variant2 (890 Chaohu) for Ningbo, recording Variant3 and Variant4 as free for Djibouti or a 904 stand-in;
- 901 Variant1 (965);
- 056A Variant1 and Variant2; 054A p5 one named variant; 055 not Variant4; 052D p3 not Variant9; 052D p1 not Variant5; 956E Variant1; Kilo Variant1.
List them in named_assets.

